# Why Carve Instead Of Markdown

Markdown is familiar, but its dialect surface makes technical documentation easy to misread. CarvePress chooses Carve because the syntax is explicit enough for the engine and linter to catch silent failures.

For example, Carve bold is `*bold*`, emphasis is `/italic/`, underline is `_underline_`, strike is `~strike~`, and highlight is `=highlight=`. A Markdown habit like `**bold**` is not accepted as a synonym; it renders as literal text and `carve lint` reports it.

The [Carve Syntax](/guide/carve-syntax) page shows the important differences as live compare blocks.
